            <ArticleTitle>MR appearance of anomalous insertion of the medial meniscus. A case report.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>554-6</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>We report on the MR imaging of an anomalous medial meniscus with a tear in a 41-year-old man. Anomaly of the medial meniscus is rare and difficult to diagnose clinically. The MR images contributed to the pre-arthroscopic diagnosis and arthroscopy confirmed the lesion. The anomalous meniscus was not related to the symptoms.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
